{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792935275,"nonce":"pr7+krvVmnZ1ENg0Dgg2Qx9PKgY=","title":"caribou run: run settings in the project and a serve tools can drive","message":"Part of 5ed625d51a511b21c35b0b711cf6ddb898831a2fa7bccabc1ecf3bb1973d123a (the project format RayDE opens).\n\nAn IDE and the CLI should run a project the same way.\n\n```toml\n[run]\npreset = \"application\"   # caribou's tier presets\nargs = [\"--level\", \"1\"]\n```\n\n- **`[run]`.** `caribou run \u003cname\u003e.cbproj` applies `preset` and `args`.\n  A `--preset` flag, and arguments on the command line, override them.\n  `--mode` stays a CLI-only debugging flag.\n- **`caribou serve`.** Under `--diagnostics json`, its first stdout line\n  is `{\"serving\":\"http://localhost:8080\"}`, once it is listening. It runs\n  until it is signalled, and stops cleanly on SIGINT or SIGTERM.\n- **Exit codes.** Every command exits nonzero on failure: a compile error, a\n  failed load, or an uncaught error in the program.","files":null}]}